                  "name": "transcriptText",
                  "fill": "$text-disabled",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": 313,
                  "content": "As you make your way north along Montgomery Street, take a moment to look up at the buildings around you. This neighborhood has reinvented itself more times than most cities manage in a lifetime. From the rubble of the 1906 earthquake rose an ambitious new financial district, and the streets you're walking now were once lined with makeshift shelters for displaced residents. Notice how the buildings gradually give way to more residential blocks as you approach Telegraph Hill. The parrots you might hear chattering overhead are the famous wild parrots of Telegraph Hill — a flock of cherry-headed conures that have called this neighborhood home since the 1990s.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.8,
                  "fontFamily": "Inter",
                  "fontSize": 16,
